1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,195
Imagine building an app by describing what you want

2
00:00:03,195 --> 00:00:06,390
in plain English, instead of writing every line of

3
00:00:06,390 --> 00:00:09,585
code yourself. An AI assistant generates the code, you

4
00:00:09,585 --> 00:00:12,780
run it, explain what is wrong, and ask for

5
00:00:12,780 --> 00:00:15,975
changes. That approach is commonly called vibe coding. It

6
00:00:15,975 --> 00:00:19,170
can make software creation more accessible, but there is

7
00:00:19,170 --> 00:00:22,365
an important catch: code that looks right is not

8
00:00:22,365 --> 00:00:23,785
necessarily code that works.

9
00:00:24,185 --> 00:00:27,589
Here is the basic workflow. First, describe the problem

10
00:00:27,589 --> 00:00:30,993
and what the finished app should do. Second, ask

11
00:00:30,993 --> 00:00:34,396
the AI to generate a solution. Third, run the

12
00:00:34,396 --> 00:00:37,800
code and observe what actually happens. Fourth, give the

13
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:41,204
AI specific feedback and improve the result. You repeat

14
00:00:41,204 --> 00:00:44,608
that cycle until the software behaves as expected. Think

15
00:00:44,608 --> 00:00:48,011
of the AI as a coding assistant, not a

16
00:00:48,011 --> 00:00:48,768
magic button.

17
00:00:49,168 --> 00:00:52,369
Suppose you want a simple task list. You could

18
00:00:52,369 --> 00:00:55,570
prompt an AI: build a web page where I

19
00:00:55,570 --> 00:00:58,771
can add tasks, mark them complete, and remove them.

20
00:00:58,771 --> 00:01:01,972
Keep the design simple, explain the files you create,

21
00:01:01,972 --> 00:01:05,174
and tell me how to run the app. The

22
00:01:05,174 --> 00:01:08,375
AI may generate HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. You open

23
00:01:08,375 --> 00:01:11,576
the page, try adding a task, and check whether

24
00:01:11,576 --> 00:01:13,710
every button does what you requested.

25
00:01:14,110 --> 00:01:17,886
Vibe coding can help beginners turn ideas into prototypes,

26
00:01:17,886 --> 00:01:21,661
help experienced developers explore options quickly, and reduce the

27
00:01:21,661 --> 00:01:25,437
amount of repetitive code people write by hand. It

28
00:01:25,437 --> 00:01:29,212
is especially useful for experimenting and learning. But speed

29
00:01:29,212 --> 00:01:32,988
during the first draft does not guarantee quality when

30
00:01:32,988 --> 00:01:36,763
the project becomes larger, more complex, or important to

31
00:01:36,763 --> 00:01:37,602
other people.

32
00:01:38,002 --> 00:01:41,499
Here is where you need to be careful. AI

33
00:01:41,499 --> 00:01:44,995
can produce bugs, misunderstand requirements, use unsafe patterns, or

34
00:01:44,995 --> 00:01:48,491
introduce unnecessary dependencies. A feature may work in one

35
00:01:48,491 --> 00:01:51,987
example and fail in another. You might also end

36
00:01:51,987 --> 00:01:55,483
up with code you cannot explain or maintain. And

37
00:01:55,483 --> 00:01:58,980
you should never paste passwords, private API keys, or

38
00:01:58,980 --> 00:02:02,476
confidential information into an AI tool without understanding its

39
00:02:02,476 --> 00:02:03,253
data policies.

40
00:02:03,653 --> 00:02:07,345
So how do you use it responsibly? Break a

41
00:02:07,345 --> 00:02:11,037
large idea into small tasks. Ask the AI to

42
00:02:11,037 --> 00:02:14,729
explain important changes. Read the code differences before accepting

43
00:02:14,729 --> 00:02:18,421
them. Run tests, try unusual inputs, and keep your

44
00:02:18,421 --> 00:02:22,113
work under version control with Git so you can

45
00:02:22,113 --> 00:02:25,805
review changes and recover earlier versions. Before deploying, check

46
00:02:25,805 --> 00:02:29,497
security and configuration carefully. For a real application, you

47
00:02:29,497 --> 00:02:32,369
remain responsible for the code you ship.

48
00:02:32,769 --> 00:02:36,418
The key lesson is simple. Vibe coding lets you

49
00:02:36,418 --> 00:02:40,067
describe an idea and collaborate with AI to create

50
00:02:40,067 --> 00:02:43,717
software faster. That is powerful, but generating code is

51
00:02:43,717 --> 00:02:47,366
only one part of engineering. Reliable software also requires

52
00:02:47,366 --> 00:02:51,016
understanding, testing, security, and maintenance. Learn to use AI

53
00:02:51,016 --> 00:02:54,665
to accelerate your thinking, not replace it. Next, we

54
00:02:54,665 --> 00:02:58,315
will explore how the internet works and how information

55
00:02:58,315 --> 00:02:59,531
travels between devices.

56
00:02:59,931 --> 00:03:03,174
If this helped you understand vibe coding, subscribe to

57
00:03:03,174 --> 00:03:06,418
Concept in Motion and comment with the technology you

58
00:03:06,418 --> 00:03:09,661
want explained next. Keep experimenting, keep learning, and always

59
00:03:09,661 --> 00:03:12,904
test what you build. See you in the next

60
00:03:12,904 --> 00:03:13,265
video.

